WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.341 --> 00:00:09.965
Every day, people get up, go to school or work, walk, read, and do many other things.

2
00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:11.927
Where do we get the energy?

3
00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:19.331
The answer lies in what we eat, drink, and breathe; our fuel is food, water, and air.

4
00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:22.132
But what about non-living things?

5
00:00:22.953 --> 00:00:23.973
What powers a car?

6
00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:25.934
What makes water boil?

7
00:00:26.475 --> 00:00:28.436
Where does your computer get its energy from?

8
00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:35.058
"I put gasoline in the car, cook over a gas stove, and plug in the computer," you reply.

9
00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:42.501
Your answer sums up the main energy sources that power non-living things: oil, gas, and electricity.

10
00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:50.945
Oil and gas have two energy uses; the first is to fuel cars, buses, trains, and planes, and

11
00:00:50.985 --> 00:00:53.226
the second is to generate electricity.

12
00:00:54.026 --> 00:01:00.749
Coal, nuclear power, and hydropower (energy from flowing water) are also used to make electricity.

13
00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:06.031
People in most developed countries use oil for 50% of their energy.

14
00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:12.073
Problems arise, however, when we rely so heavily on oil for our energy needs.

15
00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:15.695
First of all, there is a limited supply of oil.

16
00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:22.477
Oil industry experts estimate that current oil reserves will last for only forty more years.

17
00:01:23.578 --> 00:01:29.761
This means that by 2045, there will be no more oil to make gasoline or electricity.

18
00:01:30.622 --> 00:01:35.606
Currently, most of the world's available oil is consumed only by developed countries.

19
00:01:36.566 --> 00:01:44.393
Nearly a third of the world's population of 6.1 billion people has no electricity, and another third has

20
00:01:44.473 --> 00:01:46.415
only limited access to electricity.

21
00:01:47.295 --> 00:01:52.400
Twenty percent of the world's population consumes seventy percent of the world's energy resources.

22
00:01:53.621 --> 00:01:57.544
What will happen when developing countries get access to electricity and oil?

23
00:01:58.156 --> 00:01:59.517
There simply won't be enough.

24
00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:03.238
Another problem is the location of our energy.

25
00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:10.521
As recently as a couple of centuries ago, virtually everyone used fuel that they could find close to

26
00:02:10.561 --> 00:02:17.364
home. In the modern world, energy sources are often long distances away from the end user.

27
00:02:18.244 --> 00:02:23.046
For example, many countries have no oil reserves and import all of their oil.

28
00:02:24.087 --> 00:02:30.621
When oil is transported over long distances, there is the risk of oil spills, which can cause irreversible

29
00:02:30.661 --> 00:02:32.362
damage to the natural environment.

30
00:02:33.363 --> 00:02:38.905
Conflicts, or even wars, can erupt over the control of oil fields and oil pipelines.

31
00:02:40.385 --> 00:02:44.487
The most serious problem with burning oil for energy is global warming.

32
00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:51.630
The earth's atmosphere is getting hotter because there is too much carbon dioxide (CO2) in the air.

33
00:02:52.850 --> 00:03:01.219
Burning fuels like gasoline (to drive cars) and coal (to produce electricity) releases large amounts of CO2 into

34
00:03:01.259 --> 00:03:01.659
the air.

35
00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:10.405
Scientists predict that global warming may cause sea levels to rise, animals to become extinct, and extreme weather,

36
00:03:10.925 --> 00:03:13.267
everything from severe droughts to hurricanes.

37
00:03:14.808 --> 00:03:19.851
The good news is that we don't have to use oil, gas, and coal to produce energy.

38
00:03:21.112 --> 00:03:28.164
There are other energy sources that won't run out, don't require transportation across the globe, and don't release

39
00:03:28.224 --> 00:03:36.127
CO2. The best thing about energy from these alternative energy sources, also called "renewable energy," is that it

40
00:03:36.207 --> 00:03:40.028
is unlimited─it comes from water, wind, and the sun.

41
00:03:41.268 --> 00:03:46.429
Wind power is not new; boats and ships have been using it for thousands of years to travel

42
00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:47.390
across the globe.

43
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:54.011
Windmills in Europe have used wind for centuries to pump water, grind grain, and saw wood.

44
00:03:55.292 --> 00:04:02.189
In modern times, machines called wind turbines, with blades from one meter to one hundred meters long, turn

45
00:04:02.229 --> 00:04:03.510
wind into electricity.

46
00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:11.517
Scientists believe that if collections of these turbines were installed in wind farms in the world's windiest places,

47
00:04:12.197 --> 00:04:15.000
there would be enough energy to satisfy global demand.

48
00:04:16.401 --> 00:04:18.362
Solar power is energy from the sun.

49
00:04:19.523 --> 00:04:24.828
Energy from the sun can be used in two ways: to make electricity and to heat water.

50
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:30.863
Solar cells are thin pieces of silicon that produce electricity when exposed to sunlight.

51
00:04:31.684 --> 00:04:34.586
You may have used a solar-powered calculator or flashlight.

52
00:04:35.487 --> 00:04:38.048
Solar cells can also power lights in a home.

53
00:04:39.069 --> 00:04:41.691
A solar-powered car has even been built!

54
00:04:42.772 --> 00:04:47.935
In Australia, a solar boat was showcased at the 2000 Olympic Games in Sydney.

55
00:04:48.996 --> 00:04:56.529
The Solar Sailor is powered by solar panels, and its movable, wing-like solar panels also function as sails.

56
00:04:57.589 --> 00:05:01.251
The sun's energy can also heat water efficiently and cheaply.

57
00:05:02.411 --> 00:05:08.474
Water is passed through solar collectors that concentrate the sun's rays and heat the water; the hot water

58
00:05:08.554 --> 00:05:12.716
is then stored in a tank and can be used for bathing or washing dishes.

59
00:05:14.557 --> 00:05:17.538
Other kinds of renewable energy are also under development.

60
00:05:18.738 --> 00:05:22.160
One of these comes from biomass, which means organic matter.

61
00:05:23.272 --> 00:05:29.535
Wood has been used for thousands of years to create energy, but scientists have discovered that other kinds

62
00:05:29.576 --> 00:05:37.220
of organic matter can also be used to create fuel, like certain grasses, trees, plants, or even animal

63
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:44.063
dung. Biomass can be treated and made into fuel, or it can produce electricity as it decomposes.

64
00:05:45.424 --> 00:05:51.227
Another renewable energy source is geothermal energy, energy that comes from inside the earth.

65
00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:57.972
For example, steam from geysers and water from hot springs can be used to generate electricity.

66
00:05:59.253 --> 00:06:05.358
At geothermal power plants in California, geysers produce steam, which turns electric turbines.

67
00:06:06.219 --> 00:06:09.781
Some of these power generators have been operating for over forty years.

68
00:06:11.063 --> 00:06:16.207
Hydrogen is a source of clean energy that is very attractive because it is the most abundant element

69
00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:16.927
in the universe.

70
00:06:18.368 --> 00:06:25.441
A fuel cell combines hydrogen and oxygen to produce electricity and heat─and the only by-product is pure water!

71
00:06:26.581 --> 00:06:32.044
Hydrogen fuel cells have the potential to replace the engines in vehicles and provide power for cars and

72
00:06:32.084 --> 00:06:39.327
buses. Many portable devices could also be powered by these fuel cells, such as laptop computers and cell

73
00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:44.849
phones. A final type of alternative energy source under development is compressed air.

74
00:06:45.749 --> 00:06:50.231
Compressed air is the energy source for the "air car," which uses no gasoline.

75
00:06:51.492 --> 00:06:54.670
Instead, a tank full of compressed air powers the engine.

76
00:06:55.691 --> 00:06:58.313
The tank needs to be refilled at an "air" station.

77
00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:04.518
An air car factory has already been established in France, and production will begin soon.

78
00:07:05.979 --> 00:07:13.385
So, if energy from oil, coal, and gas causes problems like pollution and global warming, to name only

79
00:07:13.445 --> 00:07:17.288
a few, why don't we switch to renewable energy immediately?

80
00:07:18.369 --> 00:07:21.452
Why doesn't every house have solar-heated hot water?

81
00:07:22.516 --> 00:07:25.217
Why aren't our computers powered by wind turbines?

82
00:07:26.438 --> 00:07:28.458
Why doesn't everyone drive an air car?

83
00:07:29.779 --> 00:07:31.220
There are a number of reasons.

84
00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:37.102
First, renewable energy is currently more expensive than traditional fuels.

85
00:07:38.262 --> 00:07:44.185
Second, decades of access to cheap oil have made consumers lazy and apathetic about energy.

86
00:07:44.205 --> 00:07:48.426
"There's enough oil now, who cares about the future?"

87
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:54.773
and "As long as my city isn't polluted, it's okay," are common attitudes.

88
00:07:55.894 --> 00:08:02.236
Third, at present, the disadvantages of oil are still not grave enough to force citizens or governments to

89
00:08:02.296 --> 00:08:10.860
react. Pollution is an ever-increasing problem, but its effects are gradual, and the most severe effects of global

90
00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.821
warming may not be seen for another fifty years.

91
00:08:15.582 --> 00:08:23.207
Finally, companies and governments in the world's most industrialized nations currently earn large profits from the oil, coal,

92
00:08:23.547 --> 00:08:24.648
and gas industries.

93
00:08:25.949 --> 00:08:31.374
It is not in their interest to switch to renewable energy sources unless the public demands it.

94
00:08:32.395 --> 00:08:36.919
The good news, however, is that many people around the world are changing their habits.

95
00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:45.247
For example, some schools, community groups, and small businesses are using wind turbines and solar panels as their

96
00:08:45.307 --> 00:08:46.468
sources of electricity.

97
00:08:47.316 --> 00:08:53.758
Governments are slowly changing regulations to make it easier for builders to construct homes that rely on renewable

98
00:08:53.818 --> 00:09:00.180
energy. The earth has taken good care of us─it gives us clean air, water, and food to eat.

99
00:09:01.161 --> 00:09:05.702
By switching to renewable sources of energy, we can start to take care of the earth.
